│ patch_name               │ productive_branch_allocation                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Keep a small archive of distinct promising networks and track how often each branch       │
│                          │ produces an improvement. Cap each descent’s 2-exchange scan so one branch cannot consume  │
│                          │ the entire LP budget; then allocate subsequent searches more often to branches with       │
│                          │ better improvement histories, while still occasionally exploring less-proven branches.    │
│                          │ This applies the branch-productivity recommendation and replaces the current best-only    │
│                          │ kick loop, which repeatedly searches around the incumbent and can neglect other useful    │
│                          │ starting networks.                                                                        │
