│ patch_description        │ The current LP batch is chosen almost entirely by surrogate energy, so its calls can      │
│                          │ cluster around near-duplicate topologies and miss useful alternatives. Select             │
│                          │ energy-ranked proposals while first enforcing a minimum edge-set distance; then fill      │
│                          │ remaining slots by energy rank. Also fix the progress check: `evaluate` updates           │
│                          │ `best_score`, so comparing the returned value against `best_score` immediately afterward  │
│                          │ can never detect a new best. Comparing against the score before evaluation lets the       │
│                          │ search reset its stale counter when it actually improves.                                 │
