│ patch_name               │ price_ranked_archive                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Rather than repeatedly descending from one incumbent, this approach keeps a small,        │
│                          │ diverse archive of evaluated networks and allocates LP calls in ranked batches. It        │
│                          │ borrows the useful bottleneck-price signal and surrogate energy from earlier approaches,  │
│                          │ but combines them with an archive-based search: candidate switches are ranked by          │
│                          │ directional price relief and energy, while a separate slice of each batch preserves       │
│                          │ exploration. Promising networks are retained based on both LP quality and edge-set        │
│                          │ diversity, giving the search more chances to leave a local basin. Repaired QAOA samples   │
│                          │ seed the archive, and multi-switch perturbations provide fallback proposals when ordinary │
│                          │ switches are exhausted.                                                                   │
