│ patch_name               │ archivekick                                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current search uses an annealing state and a small archive, but its periodic reset    │
│                          │ can repeatedly revisit elite networks, and its fixed move batch may spend calls on        │
│                          │ surrogate-ranked neighbors without enough deliberate basin changes. This version keeps a  │
│                          │ diverse, bounded archive and triggers a kick from a non-elite member after 45 iterations  │
│                          │ without improvement. Kick sizes grow from 2 to 6 switches as stagnation continues, then   │
│                          │ reset on an incumbent improvement.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It seeds LP evaluations from a diversified subset of the best-energy repairs, searches    │
│                          │ bottleneck-focused 2-switches plus sampled 3-cycles, and uses batches of 8                │
│                          │ surrogate-ranked moves with up to 3 exploratory moves. The archive has 16 entries, and    │
│                          │ selection balances score and structural diversity. All LP use is budget-checked; cached   │
│                          │ or already-scored networks are skipped.                                                   │
