│ patch_description        │ The current iterated search always kicks from the incumbent, which can repeatedly revisit │
│                          │ the same basin. Keep a small archive of strong, structurally distinct networks and, after │
│                          │ sustained stagnation, launch bounded kicks from a non-elite archive member. Increase kick │
│                          │ size gradually with further stagnation, then locally descend as before. This adds basin   │
│                          │ changes without replacing the incumbent-focused search or spending extra LP calls on the  │
│                          │ kick itself; only the resulting valid network and descent proposals are scored.           │
