│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ stall_escalated_rotations                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current search samples the same fixed number of targeted rotations for every parent,  │
│                          │ even when a parent has repeatedly failed to produce an improvement. Track consecutive     │
│                          │ unproductive batches per parent and escalate the number of rotation triples only for      │
│                          │ stalled parents. Reserve some batch slots for the best-ranked rotation proposals at high  │
│                          │ stall levels, so escalation actually spends LP calls on those moves rather than letting   │
│                          │ them be crowded out by switches. Reset the stall count when the parent’s batch finds a    │
│                          │ new incumbent. This directs more exploratory effort toward difficult basins while         │
│                          │ preserving the usual switch-heavy search elsewhere.                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 6                                                                                         │
