│                          │ to improve that parent. The existing global kick size does not distinguish a repeatedly   │
│                          │ exhausted basin from a newly selected parent; a per-parent failure count does. After      │
│                          │ several unsuccessful batches, this increases the move-generation effort (including        │
│                          │ rotations involving priced links), while successful parents reset their count. The        │
│                          │ escalation is capped to keep proposal-generation time bounded.                            │
