│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_dual_search                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This version treats each promising network as a search parent and allocates LP            │
│                          │ evaluations according to both its historical productivity and its structural diversity.   │
│                          │ Parents that produce incumbent improvements receive more attention, while under-tested    │
│                          │ and distant parents retain a guaranteed exploration chance.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For each parent, the search prioritizes degree-preserving two-switches that remove        │
│                          │ bottleneck links, using dual prices and QUBO energy as inexpensive filters. It also       │
│                          │ samples three-link rotations and occasional random switches to escape local structure. A  │
│                          │ small batch is evaluated per visit so that poor parents do not consume the budget in one  │
│                          │ burst; every valid, uncached evaluation can update a diverse elite archive. Initial       │
│                          │ repaired candidates are likewise ranked by energy while preserving structural variety.    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0032                                                                                   │
