│ patch_name               │ adaptive_neighborhood_diversity                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current neighborhood screen always spends its first nine LP evaluations on the same   │
│                          │ energy-first ordering. When those moves are topologically similar, that can waste         │
│                          │ evaluations exploring nearly identical changes. Measure pairwise topology distance among  │
│                          │ the 40 best surrogate-ranked moves and adapt the initial batch: use more far-apart        │
│                          │ representatives when the pool is clustered, and retain more energy-ranked moves when it   │
│                          │ is already diverse. Keep the existing dual-guided and random reservations afterward, so   │
│                          │ this changes only the energy/diversity portion of screening.                              │
