│ patch_description        │ Track whether evaluated 2-switches or 3-link rotations improve the incumbent, then adapt  │
│                          │ the number of sampled rotations while keeping a minimum rotation mix. Rotations can       │
│                          │ escape basins that are difficult to reach through a single switch, but spending many      │
│                          │ proposals on them is wasteful when they have not helped. This change uses observed LP     │
│                          │ outcomes—not just proposal counts—to adjust their sampling rate, while retaining the      │
│                          │ existing switch search and batch ranking. Improvement is measured against the incumbent   │
│                          │ before each batch so that the reward is attributed correctly.                             │
